{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-120451",
    "CVE-2026-120452"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that libgphoto2 did not properly manage memory when\ninitializing certain cameras. If a user were tricked into connecting a\nmalicious USB device, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nlibgphoto2 to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute\narbitrary code. (CVE-2026-120451)\n\nIt was discovered that libgphoto2 did not properly manage memory when\nprocessing certain thumbnails. If a user were tricked into connecting a\nmalicious USB device, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nlibgphoto2 to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or expose sensitive\ninformation. (CVE-2026-120452)",
  "id": "USN-9017-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in libgphoto2.",
